      "message": "Updated in PS2. Since HttpAuthMethod is package-private, Apache now uses HttpTransport.isAuthenticationSchemeSupported(String) to derive the names from Type.values() and getSchemeName(), excluding NONE.\n\nThe query lives on HttpTransport because entering through a static declared on TransportHttp can expose the existing Transport/TransportHttp initialization cycle and leave HTTP/HTTPS/FTP unregistered. Separate-JVM checks pass with HttpTransport, and the new isolated-classloader test fails with the TransportHttp alternative and passes with this placement.\n\nIf you\u0027d rather avoid a new public method, I can retain the literals with a comment pointing to HttpAuthMethod.Type.\n\nThe focused HTTP and core authentication tests pass, along with the targeted core/Apache build, Javadoc generation, and API comparisons.",
